      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) It can be either a validation error (from the frontend) or an out-of-memory error (from the backend), it depends on what calling CreateBufferInternal gave us. Maybe adding context is redundant, I\u0027m not sure.\n\n2) This took me ages to figure out: We\u0027re trying to emulate what the wire (and the spec\u0027s client-server model) does - mappedAtCreation allocates on the client before we send anything to the server, so it always fails first. But in dawn native we can\u0027t actually do things in that order, because the mappedAtCreation mapping could actually be the *real* mapping. So we shuffle the error reporting around to make it look the same.",
